{
  "version": 3,
  "title": "What if you could turn invisible?",
  "series": "Field Study / The Invisible Eye",
  "pacing": "micro",
  "narration": "What if you could turn invisible? Okay. Stand in front of these stripes. Now imagine light goes straight through every part of you. See that stripe where your face used to be? Everyone else sees the wall. Great trick. One problem. What do you see? Look at this lamp. Normally, light from it enters your eye. Your lens focuses that light onto your retina. Tiny cells absorb it. That's how you know the lamp is on. Now make the whole eye invisible. The light goes straight through. The lamp is still on. You just can't see it. Keep your eyes working instead? Then some light has to stop there. Congratulations. You're a pair of eyes in the middle of the room.",
  "voiceover": "episodes/invisible-voice.wav",
  "music": {
    "track": "episodes/invisible-score.wav",
    "volume": 0.37
  },
